WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.319
There are all kinds of claims about
the red wine compound reseveratrol.

00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:08.040
In this 4-video series
I dive into the research

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.872
as to the potential benefits and side-
effects of resveratrol supplementation.

00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:20.220
"Does Resveratrol Make You Live Longer?"

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.160
Resveratrol, known as
the red wine molecule,

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.380
became a household word in 1991

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.080
when a scientist
from Bordeaux University

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.900
appeared on the popular TV show
"60 Minutes"

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.720
and attributed
the so-called French Paradox

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.300
to the French habit
of drinking red wine.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.360
The term "French Paradox"
itself

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.160
was coined in the newsletter

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.440
of the International
Organization of Vine and Wine

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.960
to explain a curious finding.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.000
If you chart death
from heart attack

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.620
versus the amount
of saturated fat

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.240
and cholesterol consumed
in different countries,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.980
there appears to be
a straight line.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.560
The more animal-based foods
populations eat,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.180
the higher their death rates
appear to be.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.700
However, two countries
didn't fall in line

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.720
with that straight line.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.360
Finland seemed to be doing
worse than expected,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.760
and France appeared to be doing
better than expected.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.680
Hence, the paradox.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.900
How could France
have saturated fat

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.460
and cholesterol intake
similar to Finland,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.980
but five times fewer
fatal heart attacks?

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.100
Everyone had their pet theories
to explain the paradox.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.420
Was it the wining?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.440
Was it the dining?

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.600
Yes, animal foods
are associated

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.160
with coronary heart disease
mortality,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.380
but plant foods
appear to be protective.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.120
So, might the fact
that the French were eating

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.560
four times as many vegetables

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.540
help account
for their lower death rates?

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.220
It turns out, however,

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.040
that there may be
no paradox at all.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.080
According to an investigation

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.220
by the World Health
Organization,

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.860
French physicians were
just under-reporting

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.260
heart disease deaths
on the death certificates.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.060
So, if you correct for that,

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.700
France basically comes
right back in line

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.380
with the death
versus animal fat

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.480
and death
versus cholesterol lines,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.520
with about four times
the fatal heart attack rates

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.700
as Japan and about four times
the animal fat consumption.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.920
By the time of the correction,
however,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.500
resveratrol research
had already taken root,

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.240
culminating in more than 17,000

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.040
scientific publications to date.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.520
But only about 1 to 2 percent
of the published reports

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.140
were human clinical trials,

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.660
and after many millions
of dollars spent

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.400
and many years
of disappointing results,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.860
the scientific tide
started to turn.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.580
Reviews began to ask whether
resveratrol was a molecule

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.500
whose time had come and gone:

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.020
"Should we now consign
resveratrol

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.940
to our intellectual
garbage cans

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.080
and move on to better things?"

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.360
Of course,
it didn't help matters

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.475
when a leading
resveratrol researcher

00:02:32.475 --> 00:02:36.060
was found guilty of 145 counts
of fabrication

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.980
and falsification of data,

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.560
throwing the whole field
into turmoil.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.000
But in 2013, resveratrol
was primed to make a comeback

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.760
with the apparent confirmation
that it was a STAC,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.400
a sirtuin-activating compound,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.460
that is, a compound
that purportedly activates

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.080
a longevity enzyme.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.960
This has been called
into question, though.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:03.060
Commentaries with titles like
"Is resveratrol an imposter?"

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.760
"Promising therapeutic,
or hopeless illusion?"

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.820
and "The resveratrol fiasco"
were published,

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.280
suggesting that the seeming
sirtuin activity

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.340
was probably the result
of experimental artifacts.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.360
"In summary," a recent review
concluded, "the jury is out."

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.040
The proof is in the pudding,
though.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.800
Does resveratrol enhance
longevity or not?

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.980
Yeast is the big success story,

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.320
with resveratrol
extending the lifespan

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.240
of brewer's yeast
by up to 70 percent.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.600
Resveratrol also helped
microscopic roundworms

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.180
live longer,
but it failed fruit flies,

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.420
mosquitoes, and water fleas.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.960
Anything bigger than
a unicellular fungus

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.340
or a microscopic worm?

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.880
Yes, resveratrol can extend
the lives of honeybees

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.340
and, most excitingly,
two vertebrates,

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.600
short-lived fish:

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.360
Gunther's
and turquoise killifish.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.720
Unfortunately, most studies
on mammals (mostly mice)

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.060
failed to show
a lifespan benefit.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.760
Resveratrol is said
to extend the life

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.200
of so-called model organisms

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.240
by mimicking
calorie restriction,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.980
but flies and mice show

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.740
robust life-extension responses
to dietary restriction,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.500
yet don't seem responsive
to resveratrol.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.380
That may just be true
of healthy animals, though.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.140
Give resveratrol to mice
in extremis,

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.420
whether bombarded by radiation,

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.860
poisoned with endotoxins,

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.900
or having their intestines
punctured

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.580
to cause sepsis-induced
kidney failure,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.100
and they do survive longer
with resveratrol

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.560
than they otherwise would
under those circumstances.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.740
Resveratrol
can also help mediate

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.980
the life-shortening effects
of high-fat diets in mice.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.500
The lifespans
of healthy mice and rats

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.320
fed normal diets are not
affected by resveratrol,

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.060
but the compound
partially prevented

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.180
the premature deaths of mice
fed high-fat diets.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.600
The authors of a meta-analysis
of the effect of resveratrol

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.520
on longevity across species
concluded

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.680
that, based on the fact
that most mouse studies

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.760
failed to show a benefit,

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.300
it's "inappropriate
for resveratrol to be marketed

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.100
as a life-extending
health supplement."

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.040
True, no study has demonstrated

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.580
resveratrol lifespan extension
in healthy rodents,

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.880
only in "metabolically
compromised mammals,"

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.700
but isn't that
a pretty accurate description

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.220
of most of the U.S. population
these days?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.580
Studies on monkeys fed diets
high in butterfat and sugar

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.380
found that resveratrol
decreased

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.540
artery and abdominal fat
inflammation.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.060
Combined with the shift
towards normalizing

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.640
the lifespans of mice
on high-fat diets,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.320
pharmacology journal
commentaries

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.280
were published with titles

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.460
like "Resveratrol—pills
to replace a healthy diet?"

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.360
speculating whether
"resveratrol is the compound

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.520
that will allow us to be
more and more inactive

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.960
while eating too much
in general

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.180
and too much fat and sugar
in particular."

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.140
Yes, a nutrition journal
editorial entitled

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.960
"Dodging physical activity
and a healthy diet" conceded,

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.820
exercise and dietary
modification

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.060
are the "most potent, cheapest,
and easiest ways

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.520
to prevent lifestyle-related
chronic diseases,"

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.500
but might resveratrol
on its own

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.660
"take the edge
off the consequences

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:04.620
of your lifestyle?"

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.580
No wonder annual sales
of resveratrol supplements

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:10.800
reached $30 million
in the U.S. alone.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.960
Approaching the peak
in interest

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.840
around the time Oprah Winfrey
mentioned it in 2009,

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.180
it was estimated
that two-thirds of people

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.260
in the United States taking

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.420
multiple daily
dietary supplement regimens

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:22.800
included resveratrol.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.880
But what does
the human data show?

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.240
I'll cover that, next.

